# Hostname egress allowlist for the DEFAULT dev-container profile.
#
# The format, the fnmatch matching, and the pattern shapes accepted are
# documented at the top of .devcontainer/infra/egress-allowlist, which the
# infra profile appends to this file at build time.
#
# Why these two hosts are here rather than in init-firewall.sh's ipset: both
# are Azure Front Door names that answer a different edge address per lookup,
# so an ipset entry resolved once at container start misses on most later
# requests and they fail with EHOSTUNREACH. The proxy admits a destination by
# hostname, which does not depend on the address the name resolved to at start.

# --- Playwright hosts ------------------------------------------------------
#
# The browser for the web app's browser test suite is baked into the image
# because the download redirects to storage.googleapis.com, a host outside this
# allowlist. These two hosts stay for Playwright's own version and metadata
# requests (`npx playwright install --dry-run`, the CLI's update check); a run
# that needs the download itself rebuilds the image.
cdn.playwright.dev
playwright.download.prss.microsoft.com
